<?xml version="1.0" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  Phase 9 — Sparkle update feed. Hosted via GitHub Releases: this exact
  file is re-uploaded (as an asset literally named "appcast.xml") to every
  new GitHub Release Scripts/release.sh walks you through creating, and
  Info.plist's SUFeedURL points at
  https://github.com/antoniukmewgen-byte/ReplixerMac/releases/latest/download/appcast.xml
  — GitHub's "latest" redirect always serves whatever asset with that exact
  name is attached to the most recent published (non-draft/non-prerelease)
  Release, so there's no separate web server or gh-pages branch involved.

  Each release adds ONE new <item> below (newest first — Sparkle doesn't
  strictly require ordering, but every real appcast in the wild does this,
  and it's what makes skimming this file by hand actually useful). Do NOT
  hand-edit the sparkle:edSignature/length values on an existing <item> —
  they're a cryptographic signature over the exact bytes of that release's
  .dmg; changing anything about the file after signing (even re-uploading
  it) makes Sparkle refuse to install it, which is the whole point.

  Windows parity: this is the mac equivalent of Replixer's version.json
  (UpdateService.cs) + the GitHub Release it's attached to in release.yml —
  same "tag push -> build -> publish a manifest + the update files together"
  shape, just Sparkle's own XML format instead of a hand-rolled one.
-->
